{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 10, "model_name": "mistralai/ministral-14b-instruct-2512", "content": "**A Whirlwind Journey Through Japan’s Magic**\n\nFrom Tokyo’s neon glow to Kyoto’s serene temples, my week in Japan was pure enchantment.\n\nI began in **Tokyo**, lost in the crowds of **Shinjuku** and **Shibuya**, where skyscrapers hummed alongside tiny ramen shops. A visit to **Meiji Shrine** brought quiet reflection amid towering cedars, while **Tsukiji Market** awoke early for fresh seafood and sushi so delicate it melted. At night, the **Shibuya Crossing** pulsed with energy—chaotic yet oddly beautiful.\n\nNext, the **Shinkansen** whisked me to **Kyoto**, where cherry blossoms still drifted in spring’s fading breath. Wandering **Arashiyama**, I chased monkeys in bamboo groves and watched the **Kamo River** glide beneath ancient bridges. **Fushimi Inari’s** torii gates stretched endlessly up the mountain, each one a silent prayer. A tea ceremony in **Gion** taught me mindfulness amid delicate whisked matcha—every sip a lesson in grace.\n\nThen, **Nara**, where wild deer bowed for crackers and **Todai-ji’s** giant Buddha loomed over the city. Feeding the friendly locals (sika deer) felt like stepping into a postcard.\n\nBack in Tokyo, **Asakusa’s** Senso-ji Temple offered golden doors and street stalls selling everything from yukata to lucky charms. My last night, a **robata grill** dinner in **Golden Gai**—tiny bars packed with jazz and whisky—proved Japan’s nights are just as vibrant as its days.\n\nLeaving was bittersweet. But the scent of **green tea**, the click of **train doors**, and the hush of **shoji screens** lingered—proof that some places don’t just stay with you. They shape you.", "logprobs": [{"token": "**", "logprob": -0.06550939381122589}, {"token": "A", "logprob": -0.27843376994132996}, {"token": " Wh", "logprob": -0.037113383412361145}, {"token": "irl", "logprob": -0.018043426796793938}, {"token": "wind", "logprob": -4